# No Figma Traceability Comments

When implementing or updating UI from **Figma MCP**, do **not** add comments that document Figma specs, sample copy, spacing, or node references. The code should be self-explanatory; design details belong in Figma, not in source files.

## Do Not Add

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — Figma sample text / format notes
/** Figma: `Uploaded at 23 Dec, 2025 on 09:34 PM` (day-first date, `on` before time). */

// ❌ BAD — layout/spacing copied from Figma
/** Figma: 16px padding, 12px section gaps; ID + date row; auction + status. */

// ❌ BAD — Figma node references
/** Figma: Segmented Button (node 1397-58141). Pill track at 1021px+. */
```

Also avoid inline `// Figma: …` or JSDoc lines that exist only to trace back to the design file.

## Instead

- Implement the UI directly — use existing components, tokens, and naming conventions.
- Add comments only for **non-obvious business logic** or technical constraints that are not visible in Figma.
- If format or copy rules matter, encode them in code (constants, helpers, tests) rather than comment blocks.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — no Figma comment; logic speaks for itself
export function formatBuyerDocumentUploadedLabel(iso: string | null | undefined): string {
  // ...
}
```
